      "term": "adaption",
      "partOfSpeech": "noun",
      "meaningZh": "n. 适应, 改编本, 适应性的变化, 适合",
      "en": "The theatre's new adaption of the folktale gives the youngest daughter the leading role.",
      "zh": "剧院新推出的这部民间故事改编剧，让最小的女儿成了主角。"
    },
    {
      "term": "cannister",
      "partOfSpeech": "noun",
      "meaningZh": "n. (放咖啡, 茶叶, 烟等的)小罐, 筒, [军](防毒面具的)滤毒罐",
      "en": "She kept the loose tea in a blue cannister beside the kettle.",
      "zh": "她把散装茶叶放在水壶旁边的一个蓝色小罐里。"
    },
    {
      "term": "hol",
      "partOfSpeech": "noun",
      "meaningZh": "n. <英口>假日",
      "en": "We're saving up for our hols instead of buying a new television.",
      "zh": "我们正在攒钱度假，而不是买一台新电视。"
    },
    {
      "term": "weiner",
      "partOfSpeech": "noun",
      "meaningZh": "n. （美）法兰克福香肠（等于wiener）",
      "en": "He tucked a grilled weiner into a soft roll and added mustard.",
      "zh": "他把一根烤好的法兰克福香肠夹进一个松软的面包卷里，又加了芥末酱。"
    },
    {
      "term": "dirty bomb",
      "partOfSpeech": "noun",
      "meaningZh": "n. 脏弹",
      "en": "The documentary explained why a dirty bomb is different from an atomic bomb.",
      "zh": "这部纪录片解释了脏弹为何不同于原子弹。"
    },
    {
      "term": "corn snow",
      "partOfSpeech": "noun",
      "meaningZh": "春天粒雪",
      "en": "By noon, the sun had softened the corn snow on the lower slopes.",
      "zh": "到了中午，阳光已让低处山坡上的春季粒雪变软了。"
    },
    {
      "term": "agony column",
      "partOfSpeech": "noun",
      "meaningZh": "私事广告栏",
      "en": "In 1890, she placed a notice in the newspaper's agony column asking her missing brother to write home.",
      "zh": "1890年，她在报纸的私事广告栏里登了一则启事，请失踪的兄弟写信回家。"
    },
    {
      "term": "levant",
      "partOfSpeech": "verb",
      "meaningZh": "vi. 躲债\n[法] 逃亡, 躲避, 躲债",
      "en": "The innkeeper feared that his guest would levant before settling the bill.",
      "zh": "旅店老板担心那位客人会在结账前逃走躲债。"
    },
    {
      "term": "maw",
      "partOfSpeech": "noun",
      "meaningZh": "n. (反刍动物的)第四胃, 嗉囊, (人的)胃",
      "en": "A warm meal finally quieted the rumbling in his empty maw.",
      "zh": "一顿热饭终于让他空空的胃不再咕咕叫了。"
    },
    {
      "term": "schoolmarm",
      "partOfSpeech": "noun",
      "meaningZh": "n. 女教师, 女学究",
      "en": "In 1885, the village schoolmarm taught thirty children in a single room.",
      "zh": "1885年，村里的女教师在同一间教室里教三十个孩子。"
    },
    {
      "term": "gigolo",
